  "summary_text": "Kyle, you're running hot across the portfolio. Port Washington is outperforming DOW-adjusted expectations by 2.6% MTD with 21% more appointments and 39% YoY growth; Hicksville is crushing it at +11.3% vs. expectation with 46% appointment growth and 45% revenue lift month-to-date. Hicksville's groomer productivity jumped 23% yesterday ($485 vs. $394 trailing average), signaling strong execution on the smaller floor. You should be proud of the booking momentum and capacity deployment across both legacy stores\u2014the 39% YoY comp is real growth, not calendar noise.\n\nFlag one concern: Port Washington's retail revenue collapsed 23% yesterday and is soft week-to-date, while add-ons at Hicksville dropped to 33% attach (down from 43% last week). This isn't a capacity problem\u2014it's a front-of-house and upsell discipline drift. With Columbus Day depressing Saturday bookings 10% in two days, now is not the time to leave money on the table. Retail inventory is also tight (20 out of stock at each legacy location); prioritize Shanti's Medical Journey and 6\" Bully Sticks reorders before the holiday window.\n\nGlen Cove is still a ramp (week one visibility only), but note: you have zero groomer coverage scheduled today and tomorrow. That location will produce nothing those days. Confirm whether that's intentional downtime or a scheduling gap.\n\n**Capacity & coverage:** Today you have 11 active groomer-days across Port Washington (6) and Hicksville (5) with 15.0 bather hours at PW; tomorrow drops to 4 groomer-days (Hicksville only, no bathers), then next 7 days settles at 57 total groomer-days with 83 bather hours\u2014well above trailing baseline."
